    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The database is refusing connections (access denied for all queries, including `SELECT 1`), so I cannot execute verification queries. I'll complete the investigation using the semantic-network evidence and precedent metric SQL, which is sufficient to construct the query.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2 Report\n\n### 1. Entity Semantics\n\n**Tables (investigated in depth):**\n- **SUBJECT_SUMMARY** — Subject-level summary fact table per term: one row per subject (or cluster) per term. Carries `DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `SCHOOL_NAME`, `TERM_CODE`, and `SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER` (\"Final enrollment number of the subject\"), plus weekly/credit/listener enrollment breakdowns. This is the only subject-grain fact table that natively carries **both** department name and school name plus the official `SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER`.\n- **SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY** — Subject-level rollup of section offerings per term; has `OFFER_DEPT_NAME`, `OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME`, `SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER`, `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`, `TERM_CODE`. Similar shape but represents the registrar offering rollup rather than the final enrollment summary.\n- **SUBJECT_OFFERED** — Section-level grain (one row per section); enrollment at section/subject/cluster level. Would need aggregation and risks double counting at section grain.\n- **ACADEMIC_TERMS** — Term dimension: `TERM_CODE`, `TERM_START_DATE`, `IS_CURRENT_TERM` ('Y'/'N'), `TERM_STATUS` ('Current'...). Source of the requested **term start date** and of current-term identification.\n- **ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER** — Exactly three rows resolving relative term references; `IS_CURRENT_TERM='Y'` row identifies the SIS current term. Precedent dw_4683 uses this table for \"current term\".\n- **SIS_DEPARTMENT** — Department dimension (`DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `SCHOOL_NAME`, `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING`, ...). Not strictly needed since SUBJECT_SUMMARY carries department/school names directly.\n- Other Phase-1 tables (TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, IAP_*, TIME_*, FCLT_*, HR_*, MASTER_DEPT_*, CIP*, etc.) — reviewed; they either belong to different business processes (textbook program, library reserves, IAP activities, facilities/HR domains), different granularity, or lack the required combination of `SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER` + department + school + term.\n\n**Column concept:**\n- **column_concept_enrollment_measures** — Two families: `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` (headcount snapshots) vs `SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER` (official registrar enrollment). Decision guide: *\"Questions about official subject enrollment (e.g. 'subject enrollment number greater than 10') → Use SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER.\"* The task says \"maximum **subject enrollment number**\" — a lexical match to `SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER`, and the decision guide points to SUBJECT_SUMMARY.\n\n**Concepts:**\n- **concept_subject_offering_facts** — groups SUBJECT_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_OFFERED(_SUMMARY), catalog, TIP, library tables; notes they differ in granularity and enrollment semantics.\n- **concept_academic_term_dimension** — groups ACADEMIC_TERMS, ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL, ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER; the parameter table resolves 'C' (current) references.\n- **concept_department_dimension** — SIS_DEPARTMENT / STUDENT_DEPARTMENT / SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT.\n\n**Precedent metrics:**\n- **dw_4683** — \"current term\" enrollment question; SQL pattern: `ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER p JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS t ON p.TERM_CODE=t.TERM_CODE JOIN SUBJECT_SUMMARY s ON t.TERM_CODE=s.TERM_CODE WHERE p.IS_CURRENT_TERM='Y'`, aggregating `SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER` per `DEPARTMENT_NAME` with HAVING.\n- **dw_1350** — the exact \"grand total per school\" shape: DepartmentStats CTE → SchoolRollup CTE `(NULL department, school, NULL stats, SUM of totals)` → UNION ALL, and its rollup tuple enumeration follows the SELECT-list order positionally.\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\n- SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY graph neighbors: joins to ACADEMIC_TERMS (term), SIS_DEPARTMENT, SUBJECT_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_OFFERED (section child), LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED, TIP_DETAIL, catalog tables; member of concept_subject_offering_facts; columns mapped to column_concepts term_code, subject_id, department_name, enrollment_measures, total_units, master_subject_id.\n- SUBJECT_SUMMARY joins to ACADEMIC_TERMS via TERM_CODE and to SIS_DEPARTMENT via DEPARTMENT_CODE (per column definitions); consumed by dw_4683 and many enrollment metrics.\n- ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER → ACADEMIC_TERMS via TERM_CODE (documented in column defs).\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Dimension matrix (enrollment source candidates):**\n\n| Dimension | SUBJECT_SUMMARY | SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY | SUBJECT_OFFERED |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Granularity | one row per subject per term (documented) | one row per subject per term (documented) | one row per **section** per term (documented) |\n| Measure | `SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER` = \"Final enrollment number of the subject\" | `SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER` + `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` | section/subject/cluster enrollment numbers |\n| Dept/School names | `DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `SCHOOL_NAME` native | `OFFER_DEPT_NAME`, `OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME` native | offering dept/school native |\n| Term link | `TERM_CODE` → ACADEMIC_TERMS | `TERM_CODE` → ACADEMIC_TERMS | via summary keys/TERM_CODE |\n| Fan-out risk | none at subject grain | none at subject grain | section grain duplicates subject-level values |\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness:**\n- Required measure \"maximum subject enrollment number\": SUBJECT_SUMMARY — SUPPORTED (`SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER`, decision-guide endorsed); SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY — SUPPORTED (column exists); SUBJECT_OFFERED — SUPPORTED but wrong grain (section-level rows would need dedup).\n- Required grouping keys \"department and school\": SUBJECT_SUMMARY — SUPPORTED (`DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `SCHOOL_NAME`); SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY — SUPPORTED (`OFFER_DEPT_NAME`, `OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME`).\n- Required \"current academic term\" filter: both — SUPPORTED via `TERM_CODE` join to ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER/ACADEMIC_TERMS (`IS_CURRENT_TERM='Y'`).\n- Required \"term start date\" output: ACADEMIC_TERMS.`TERM_START_DATE` — SUPPORTED (only term dimension carries it; ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER also has TERM_START_DATE).\n- HAVING max > 5: SUPPORTED on any candidate via `HAVING MAX(SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER) > 5`.\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring:**\n- \"maximum subject enrollment number\" lexically matches column `SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER` (not `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`); the column_concept decision guide explicitly anchors \"subject enrollment number\" phrasing to **SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER**.\n- \"current academic term\" anchors to `ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER.IS_CURRENT_TERM='Y'` (precedent dw_4683) and/or `ACADEMIC_TERMS.IS_CURRENT_TERM='Y'`; both resolve to the same single term code.\n- \"term start date\" anchors to `ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_START_DATE`.\n- \"department and school\" anchor to `SUBJECT_SUMMARY.DEPARTMENT_NAME` / `SCHOOL_NAME` (canonical base columns; no full-name variants requested).\n- Grand-total tuple \"(null department, school, null term start date, total max enrollment)\" positionally fixes the SELECT order as: DEPARTMENT_NAME, SCHOOL_NAME, TERM_START_DATE, MAX_SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER (same positional convention observed in precedent dw_1350's rollup description, which matched its SELECT order exactly).\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence:**\n- \"Current term + SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER per department\" precedents: 1 — dw_4683 (on SUBJECT_SUMMARY, via ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER + ACADEMIC_TERMS join chain).\n- \"Per-school grand total rollup (NULL dept, school, NULLs, total)\" precedents: 2 — dw_1350 (DepartmentStats/SchoolRollup UNION ALL pattern), dw_3904 (same tuple convention).\n\n### 4. Business Usage\n- SUBJECT_SUMMARY is the standard fact for final enrollment statistics by department/school/term (table desc; dw_4683, dw_4812, dw_1393 consume it).\n- ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER is the standard resolver for relative \"current term\" references (table desc; dw_4683, dw_3224 use it).\n- The DepartmentStats→SchoolRollup→UNION ALL pattern is the established idiom for per-school grand totals (dw_1350).\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\n- semantic_search ×2 (all types, topk=50) → screened.\n- semantic_get: SUBJECT_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, ACADEMIC_TERMS, ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER, SIS_DEPARTMENT, column_concept_enrollment_measures, dw_1350, dw_4683 ✔\n- semantic_graph query_neighbors on SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY ✔ (joins/concepts/column_concepts retrieved).\n- Remaining Phase-1 tables/concepts (catalog feeds, TIP/library, IAP, time/facilities/HR domains, other column_concepts) were screened against task requirements in Sections 1/3b: none carries the required SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER + department + school + current-term combination at subject grain, or belongs to unrelated domains (facilities, HR, CIP, Moira, buildings).\n- mysql_query: attempted 6 times — **all failed with \"Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'\"** (server-side credential issue, including for `SELECT 1`). Execution verification was therefore impossible; the SQL is built strictly on documented column definitions and precedent metric SQL.\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a. Tables/columns:**\n- **SUBJECT_SUMMARY**: `DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `SCHOOL_NAME`, `SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER`, `TERM_CODE` — decision guide explicitly anchors \"subject enrollment number\" to this table/column; native dept+school names avoid extra joins and fan-out.\n- **ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER** (`IS_CURRENT_TERM='Y'`) → **ACADEMIC_TERMS** (`TERM_CODE`, `TERM_START_DATE`) — exact join chain of precedent dw_4683 for \"current term\", and TERM_START_DATE is the requested date.\n\n**6b. SQL approach:** DepartmentStats CTE: join parameter→terms→summary, filter current term, GROUP BY department, school, term start date, `HAVING MAX(SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER) > 5`. SchoolRollup CTE: `(NULL, SCHOOL_NAME, NULL, SUM(dept max))` grouped by school (following dw_1350's rollup of post-filter department stats). UNION ALL, output order per the rollup tuple: department, school, term start date, max enrollment. No rounding applied.\n\n**6c. Three-perspective reasons:**\n- **Data**: SUBJECT_SUMMARY is one row per subject per term (no fan-out); single current term makes TERM_START_DATE constant per group; HAVING applies the >5 threshold at department level as asked.\n- **Semantic-network**: column_concept_enrollment_measures decision_guide names SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER for \"subject enrollment number\" questions; concept_academic_term_dimension documents ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER as the current-term resolver; graph edges confirm TERM_CODE joins.\n- **Business**: dw_4683 is a same-shape current-term/department/SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER precedent using the identical three-table join chain; dw_1350 is the same-shape per-school grand-total precedent (NULL-dept rollup rows via UNION ALL).\n\n**6d. Alternatives:** SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY could serve (has OFFER_DEPT_NAME/OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME/SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER), but the decision guide and dw_4683 precedent favor SUBJECT_SUMMARY for \"subject enrollment number\" wording; the tie-breaker (actual data comparison) is unavailable due to the DB access failure.\n\n**Final SQL** (built on documented schemas; live verification blocked by persistent `Access denied` server error):\n\n",
